{"id":1,"explanation":"The nonce check in verify must remain: rejecting a previously seen nonce prevents a token from being replayed. #123 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":2,"explanation":"Call ensure_key_salt before constructing KeyManager. If salt setup fails, startup must stop instead of initializing the manager.","unsure":""}
{"id":3,"explanation":"Before allocating buf with topN elements, keep topN at or below maxSimpleTopN so the resulting slice stays at or below 1 MiB. maxSimpleTopN is the named limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":4,"explanation":"When meta.abi_version is absent, abi must be None. Treating it as the current ABI could misinterpret the metadata. #1784 is the related issue; Abi::from converts a present version.","unsure":""}
{"id":5,"explanation":"TLP reads /etc/tlp.conf after files matching /etc/tlp.d/*.conf, so values there override the drop-in written at /etc/tlp.d/90-power.conf.","unsure":""}
{"id":6,"explanation":"These TLP settings require version 1.10 or later. _AC, _BAT and _SAV are profile suffixes. Leave the _AC version of this setting unset so GNOME's Performance toggle continues to work; this command sets only the _BAT version.","unsure":""}
{"id":7,"explanation":"On a JsonException, this catch block returns null. The caller is responsible for logging the warning, so this block does not log it.","unsure":""}
{"id":8,"explanation":"When an AllowedTools set is in use, RemoveSkipPermissions must remove --dangerously-skip-permissions from args. That flag bypasses the --allowedTools restriction.","unsure":""}
{"id":9,"explanation":"For the dead-code decision made by thunk_is_dead, consult the verdict table at rust/xray-core/src/compiler/graph_preamble.rs in is_definitely_dead_code. The path identifies the file and the text after the colon identifies the symbol.","unsure":""}
{"id":10,"explanation":"repos_skipped is a placeholder. Derive its value from the domains-to-repos mapping; #874 tracks that work.","unsure":""}
{"id":11,"explanation":"index.regex_query uses a linear-time DFA for this regex search, so the query does not incur regex backtracking. regex_query is the referenced method.","unsure":""}
{"id":12,"explanation":"Keep this token-family table schema in sync with RefreshTokenSqliteBackend._ensure_schema in src/storage/refresh_token_backend.py. The path identifies the file and the text after the colon identifies the class and method.","unsure":""}
{"id":13,"explanation":"MAX_BATCH is 500 because the vendor batch API accepts no more than 500 items per request. doc:vendor-api#limits points to the limits section of the vendor API documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":14,"explanation":"Keep these Status values in sync with STATUS_LABELS in web/src/status.ts. Reordering the iota entries changes their stored integer values and can make existing values mean a different status. #88 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":15,"explanation":"Keep this index's columns ordered tenant_id, then created_at, to match the orders_by_tenant query. orders_by_tenant names the query this index supports.","unsure":""}
{"id":16,"explanation":"TList.Add relies on FCount never exceeding Length(FItems). Grow must preserve that bound when expanding storage; FCount and FItems are the referenced fields, and Grow is the referenced operation.","unsure":""}
{"id":17,"explanation":"close must call _flush before closing _sink because closing drops _buf. Reversing the calls could lose buffered data. _flush, _sink and _buf identify the affected method and fields.","unsure":""}
{"id":18,"explanation":"For a path supplied by a request, resolve it under workspaceRoot and reject any .. escape outside that root. This requirement applies to the target path built from userPath; normalization alone does not show the required rejection.","unsure":""}
{"id":19,"explanation":"Drain ring before freeing buf. Otherwise an IRQ handler could still use the freed buffer, causing a use-after-free. ring_drain is the required drain operation; #2201 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":20,"explanation":"Reserve space for n items up front so ingestion needs one allocation. Repeated push_back growth previously took 40% of the measured profile. doc:perf-notes#ingest points to the ingest section of the performance notes.","unsure":""}
{"id":21,"explanation":"Use HOLDLOCK on this SQL Server MERGE into dbo.Accounts because concurrent upserts can race without it. doc:mssql-merge#concurrency points to the concurrency section of the referenced documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":22,"explanation":"The autonomous transaction lets an audit row persist even if the calling transaction rolls back. The comment explains the PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION declaration.","unsure":""}
{"id":23,"explanation":"SQLite ALTER TABLE cannot drop the needed constraints directly, so this migration creates leases_new as part of rebuilding the table. doc:sqlite-alter#otheralter points to the relevant ALTER TABLE documentation section.","unsure":""}
{"id":24,"explanation":"The loop polls every five seconds because NFS mounts do not emit the inotify events this work would need. The 5 in done.wait(5) is that interval.","unsure":""}
{"id":25,"explanation":"Keep the for...of loop when awaiting run(job). An await inside forEach would let errors escape the intended try/catch. forEach and for...of are the loop forms being compared.","unsure":""}
{"id":26,"explanation":"A frame returned by read_frame must have length at most MAX_FRAME; the decoder rejects larger frames. Vec<u8> is the frame's type, and MAX_FRAME is the named size limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":27,"explanation":"Register drainHook with addShutdownHook before calling pool.start(). The hook drains the pool on SIGTERM, so it must be installed before the pool starts.","unsure":""}
{"id":28,"explanation":"Move backoff's fixed retry delay into configuration. The task is complete when Default in internal/retry/policy.go reads that configuration; the path identifies the file and Default the symbol. The current delay is two seconds.","unsure":""}
{"id":29,"explanation":"Issue #412 contains the full matrix of transitions among the LeaseState values Active, Released and Stale.","unsure":""}
{"id":30,"explanation":"Pass the token to tool login through standard input only. Putting it in command arguments would expose it through ps, which shows argv to other users. --token-stdin selects the standard-input path.","unsure":""}
{"id":31,"explanation":"Create the app_reader role before granting it SELECT access. Migration 042 assumes that role already exists; app_reader is the role named by both statements.","unsure":""}
{"id":32,"explanation":"Make on_event idempotent because Stripe can retry a webhook for three days, so the same event may arrive more than once. doc:stripe#webhook-retries points to the webhook retry documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":33,"explanation":"Compare sig and expected with hmac.Equal. It performs a constant-time MAC comparison; using == would expose timing information.","unsure":""}
{"id":34,"explanation":"Build the CodeGraph from facts once per index. The build costs O(edges), so doing it for every query would repeat that work. CodeGraph::build is the referenced constructor.","unsure":""}
{"id":35,"explanation":"Changing the packed layout of TCustomerRec can make existing saved .dat files unreadable or misread. Bump FILE_VERSION when changing that layout; FILE_VERSION is the referenced version marker.","unsure":""}
{"id":36,"explanation":"Change MSG_MAX together with MSG_MAX_WIRE in proto/messages.h so the limits stay consistent. The path identifies the header and the text after the colon identifies its constant.","unsure":""}
{"id":37,"explanation":"After authMiddleware runs, session.userId must be non-null. The handler relies on that authentication invariant; authMiddleware is the referenced middleware.","unsure":""}
{"id":38,"explanation":"Keep the check and subsequent put under synchronized(cache) so they happen atomically. Using ConcurrentHashMap alone would not make that two-step operation atomic.","unsure":""}
{"id":39,"explanation":"Validate the user-supplied repository alias against the registry before joining it into a path. This prevents an unvalidated alias from affecting path construction. #1996 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":40,"explanation":"Payment Amount must be nonnegative. Represent refunds as separate rows with Kind = 'R', rather than as negative Amount values. Amount and Kind are the referenced columns.","unsure":""}
{"id":41,"explanation":"Set stop_ before calling worker_.join(). Otherwise the worker may never stop and join can block forever; stop_ is the stop flag and worker_ is the thread being joined.","unsure":""}
{"id":42,"explanation":"The limiter is sized around the GitHub API limit of 5,000 requests per hour per token. doc:github-rest#rate-limits points to the rate-limit documentation; the 720 millisecond interval corresponds to that hourly rate.","unsure":""}
{"id":43,"explanation":"Stop the cidx service before replacing /usr/local/bin/cidx. Replacing the binary while it is running can fail with “Text file busy.”","unsure":""}
{"id":44,"explanation":"Do not share _lease between jobs: a shared CredentialLease could expose one user's credentials to another. #77 is the related issue. This field declaration is where that sharing risk needs attention.","unsure":""}
{"id":45,"explanation":"Keep len(ids) at or below 999 when building this DELETE statement, because its bound parameters must fit the stated SQLite per-statement variable limit. ids supplies the values for the placeholders in marks.","unsure":""}
{"id":46,"explanation":"If cgroup.create(limit) fails, warn and let the job continue. The comment says containment setup can fail because of a bad memory estimate and should not abort the job.","unsure":""}
{"id":47,"explanation":"Remove the legacy /v1/jobs route registered here. #530 tracks its removal.","unsure":""}
{"id":48,"explanation":"The session model decision is documented at doc:adr-007#session-model. It explains why SessionRegistry keeps sessions per tab; adr-007 is the referenced decision document and session-model its anchor.","unsure":""}
{"id":49,"explanation":"This partial index speeds up active-lease lookups by about 30 times. Its WHERE released_at IS NULL clause indexes only unreleased leases, keyed by credential_id.","unsure":""}
{"id":50,"explanation":"Keep EVENT_TYPES in sync with EVENT_LABELS in web/src/events.ts and with docs/events.md. The first path identifies a code symbol; the second identifies the event documentation.","unsure":""}
